      "answer": "$(\\frac25,-\\frac45)$ and $(\\frac4{15},\\frac{16}{45})$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use the correct quotient or product rule — M1*.\n\nObtain a correct derivative in any form — A1, for example $\\frac{(1-3x)2x-x^2(-3)}{(1-3x)^2}=\\frac{2x-3x^2}{(1-3x)^2}$, or $3x^2(1-3x)^{-2}+2x(1-3x)^{-1}$.\n\nEquate the derivative to $8$ and solve for $x$ — DM1: $75x^2-50x+8=(15x-4)(5x-2)$.\n\nObtain $x=\\frac25$ and $x=\\frac4{15}$ — A1. Guidance: exact values required.\n\nObtain $y=-\\frac45$ and $y=\\frac{16}{45}$ — A1. Guidance: allow A1 for one correct point.\n\nTotal: 5",
